Hi Matthew and Carys,

I've attached the closeout wording for the next Fare Payments change. At this=
 morning's review Matthew and I could find records for 11 of the 14 checks, b=
ut not completion records for the fallback route confirmation, first watched =
checkout outcome or second engineer's readback. We cannot tell from the missi=
ng records whether those checks happened, so the historical gaps remain open.

For the next change, please have the change owner record the confirmed fallba=
ck route and confirmation time, and the time and observed outcome of the firs=
t watched checkout. The second engineer should enter their own name, readback=
 time and what they confirmed in the change record. A spoken all-clear is not=
 enough to close it.

Keep rollout end as its own timestamp. If either entry is still awaited, or a=
ny other required evidence is missing, leave verification and closeout open a=
nd hand over the outstanding item to duty with a named owner and next check t=
ime. That gives the next engineer someone to follow up with.

Thanks,
Daniel

